<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 72 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 72 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 72 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    550 MLN    550 MLN    600 MLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    83 MLN*    155 MLN*   =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS				 22 MLN*</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    83 MLN*    =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 1  T-BILLS				    50 MLN*</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
